finding: The public loadGltf path does not always refuse required unsupported extensions by name as stage 1 and README promise. src/index.ts resolves every buffer before parse checks extensionsRequired. EXT_meshopt_compression explicitly permits a URI-less fallback placeholder buffer when the extension is required (Khronos EXT_meshopt_compression README, fallback buffers). Independently reproducing that layout with extensionsRequired:["EXT_meshopt_compression"], a compressed data-URI buffer and a URI-less fallback buffer throws "glTF buffer has no URI or BIN chunk", not EXT_meshopt_compression. The required-Draco test only calls parse with an empty-buffer fixture and cannot catch this public loading-path failure. Validate required extensions immediately after reading JSON, before attempting unsupported buffer resolution, and cover the public loader with this layout.
